API.md §4.4 F12, ERRORS.md §1.5 (`source`), EVALUATION.md §9.2, TYPES.md §7.2: a literal map key in an amend path is stored, so it names the map field's declaration, as the same key does in a map literal; the value names it too.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Cfg {
  hs: {UInt8: UInt8}
}

local let cfg: Cfg = { hs: { 1: 1 } }
-- a/dev.layer.canon --
package a
layer dev

amend cfg {
  hs[303]: 1
  hs[2]: 304
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3201]  a/dev.layer.canon:5:6
  303 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:4 (hs: {UInt8: UInt8})

error[E3201]  a/dev.layer.canon:6:10
  304 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:4 (hs: {UInt8: UInt8})

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
